  "term": "infancy",
  "definition": "Infancy is the stage of immaturity in which a person depends on parental care, beginning at birth and lasting until biological or broader social self-support. In this historical account, the period is treated as important for development because prolonged dependence allows greater learning, flexibility, and complex mental and social growth.",
